    - target: {fileID: 158228855869665193, guid: bcefd6bd51ce47b438fb5d83f536cd3c,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: "Normal maps are special textures that store details about the direction
        of the surface, which are usually used in light calculations.\r\n\r\nThere
        are 2 different standards, OpenGL and DirectX. Unity uses OpenGL and then
        converts it to its own optimized system. This changes between versions, which
        is why a built in function is used.\r\n\r\nThe top image displays it as a
        normal albedo image while the bottom one shows it after the conversion.\r\n\r\nFuther
        information can be found in the light section.\r"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
